NCEAS six-region presence-only / presence–absence benchmark tables
=================================================================

These files are a working copy of the dataset described in:

  Elith, J., et al. (2020). Presence-only and presence-absence data for
  comparing species distribution modeling methods. *Biodiversity Informatics*
  15(2): 69–80. https://doi.org/10.17161/bi.v15i2.13384

The article and associated data are licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0):

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

Copyright remains with the original authors (Elith et al.). First publication
rights: *Biodiversity Informatics*.

You may share and adapt the material for **non-commercial** purposes, with
attribution. You may **not** use it for commercial purposes. You may **not**
apply a licence (including the MIT licence of this repository's software) that
would allow recipients to use these data commercially.

Protocol notes and independent-PA evaluation follow Valavi et al. (2022),
*Ecological Monographs*, doi:10.1002/ecm.1486. That paper's code and OSF
prediction dumps are **not** redistributed here; optional alignment summaries
under `can/valavi_*` are author-computed comparison statistics, not the OSF
prediction files.

